Z||000056||BENGAL4||08-19-2001||07:36 PM||||Had a great time yesterday. thanks to every one that attended. Here is a list of the participants.<P>87 Coupe 3.6 - 87EC0something and Fiero Wife.<BR>86GT 3.2 - Boilermaker.<BR>87GT - Mrs Boilermaker.<BR>Fearri - Turbo 2.8 Roger Garrison.<BR>86SE  3800 II S/C - John & Heather Altman.<BR>86GT - Indiana Resto Guy & Son.<BR>86GT - dlancer.<BR>87GT - Paul (non-forum member).<BR>88GT - Mike & Daughter (non-forum member).<BR>86GT 3800 II S/C - Bengal4.<P>Some of the guys took pictures. Please post them when you get them. We will do another one in September or October. I will keep you posted. Thanks again for attending.<P><BR>Bill<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000057||87ECO5||08-19-2001||08:16 PM||||Awesome time, folks!  Can't wait to do it again!<P>Did anyone get a photo of those Fiero-hating grocery carts!?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000058||rogergarrison||08-19-2001||09:18 PM||||for those not there, takes some explaining. We cruised to a Burger King at a big shopping center. A storm kicked up pretty quick with some strong winds. all these grocery carts all over the parking lot all took off and raced towards us enmass. we got them all and tipped em over. It was like a horror movie scene, we shoulda had a video camera and sent it in to funniest home video||||reg||1
